@senate_solidarist_pact_aftermath
title: A right-bloc Senate map

PiS and the social-solidarist Left sign one agreed candidate per district.
Konfederacja is left to compete on its own, while the coalition can present the
Senate as part of a broader right-wing governing compact rather than a separate
democratic bargain.

The price is obvious: the pact hardens the camp line and ties Lewica to PiS in
public. But the districts are now coordinated, and the Senate fight no longer
splinters the right side of the ballot.

- @poland_event_queue: Campaign with the allied districts

