= September 2023 — The queue behind the sealed frontier

Piotr Wawrzyk, the deputy foreign minister responsible for consular affairs,
has been dismissed as prosecutors follow intermediaries, cash and expedited
applications through Polish missions abroad. Foreign Minister Zbigniew Rau
calls the system sound. PiS still campaigns as the only party able to close a
border.

At the consulates, civil servants now answer for decisions made above them;
students, workers and families with lawful applications discover that every
visa is being discussed as evidence. Lewica can follow the patronage chain,
build the lawful system PiS neglected, or borrow the government's fear of the
people to whom its officials allegedly sold access.

- @visa_inquiry
- @visa_capacity
- @visa_auction

@visa_inquiry
title: Demand an evidence-led parliamentary and prosecutor inquiry
subtitle: Keep Wawrzyk's intermediaries, contracts and chain of command at the centre; refuse an instant migration slogan.
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "Evidence-led consular accountability"; judicial_repair_mandate += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 3; pis_relation -= 5; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left follows contracts, names and consular files"

Our deputies publish the contracts, consular posts and responsible officials
as a single line of inquiry. Wawrzyk becomes the beginning of the file rather
than a convenient ending, and Rau must defend who supervised the system.

The work is slower than an election slogan, but it leaves prosecutors and the
next Sejm a record that does not turn every visa holder into a suspect.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the consular file on the events desk

@visa_capacity
title: Pair the inquiry with lawful migration and consular capacity
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Give honest staff and applicants a rule-bound alternative while the right demands fewer visas of every kind.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No policy team can turn the scandal into an administrative alternative.
