= December 2023 — Two excluded parties, not a reborn third pole

Lewica and PSL formed the government. Poland 2050 lost both its Third Way
partner and access to office, but KO is outside beside it. That changes
Hołownia's opportunity: he cannot refound his party as an anti-KO insurgency
while sharing votes, committees and attacks on the cabinet with KO.

The two opposition caucuses coordinate on parliamentary scrutiny without
merging. KO supplies scale; Poland 2050 supplies institutional detail. There
is no automatic polling surge, green absorption or presidential bonus for
Hołownia — only the harder work of remaining visible beside a larger ally.

