= December 2023 — The excluded partner starts again

The coalition agreement admits KO, PSL and Lewica while leaving Poland 2050
outside. The Third Way bargain is over, but **Szymon Hołownia** refuses the
conclusion that his movement must now choose one of the two largest parties.

He keeps the chair and announces a second founding congress: anti-PiS because
the state cannot return to party capture, anti-KO because replacing one
patronage system with another is not renewal. Volunteers who were drifting
toward Konfederacja hear an anti-establishment offer without its nationalist
programme. Poland 2050 gains polling momentum at Konfederacja's expense.

The relaunch also gives Hołownia a real chance of surviving the leadership
reckoning after the 2025 presidential cycle. It is not immunity: a presidential
victory would still make party leadership constitutionally incompatible, and
a weak movement can still reject its founder. For now, his independence has
raised the ceiling.

This is Poland 2050's decision. Lewica can recognise an independent competitor
or defend the cabinet bargain and challenge it for the same voters.

- @p2050_comeback_channel
- @p2050_comeback_compete

@p2050_comeback_channel
title: Keep an institutional-reform channel open
subtitle: Recognise Poland 2050's independence without offering it a place in the cabinet.
on-arrival: p2050_relation += 5; ko_relation -= 1; institutional_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "Lewica opens a reform channel to Hołownia's independent movement"

Lewica offers named contacts on courts, public appointments and parliamentary
procedure. The channel cannot undo the exclusion, but it lets two competing
parties cooperate without pretending they share an electoral bloc.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the reform channel

@p2050_comeback_compete
title: Defend the coalition and contest the anti-system vote
subtitle: Treat Hołownia's relaunch as a rival campaign rather than a wounded former partner.
on-arrival: p2050_relation -= 5; anti_system_trust += 3; media_capacity += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "Lewica answers Hołownia's relaunch with its own anti-establishment case"

Lewica argues that independence is proved through votes, organisation and
delivery rather than a new founding speech. Poland 2050 keeps its comeback;
the Left refuses to leave the anti-system electorate uncontested.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the relaunch to the events desk

@p2050_greens_absorption_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — a fixed March follow-up dissolves Zieloni, guarantees Poland 2050 the first three MPs, splits larger delegations with Nowoczesna and raises Hołownia's retained leadership ceiling without giving Lewica authority over the decision.
title: Zieloni dissolve into Hołownia's movement
subtitle: Poland 2050 gains the core Green delegation while any larger caucus splits with Nowoczesna
