= December 2023 — The powder settles in the chamber

Grzegorz Braun, a Konfederacja deputy, has emptied a fire extinguisher over the
Hanukkah menorah in the Sejm and struck at a woman who tried to stop him.
Jewish guests cough in the corridor while the film is already being cut for
Braun's channels.

Deputy Marshal Krzysztof Bosak and party leader Sławomir Mentzen now have to
decide whether their federation disciplines Braun or lets him become a rival
martyr. Lewica must protect the people in the room and the chamber's rules
without building the assailant a larger stage than the act itself supplied.

- @braun_rules
- @braun_front
- @braun_ignore

@braun_rules
title: Enforce Sejm rules, document the act and demand a criminal inquiry
subtitle: Centre witnesses, medical reports and Marshal's Guard footage; leave Braun less room to turn punishment into a political spectacle.
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 4; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; minority_safety += 5; konf_braunist_share += 3; konf_mentzenite_share -= 2; konf_nationalist_share -= 1; far_right_fragmentation += 4; public_trust += 2; braun_legal_preparation += 4; news_headline = "Procedure isolates Braun without making him the chamber's protagonist"

Witness statements, the medical report and the chamber recording enter one
file. The Presidium can punish Braun for what he did, and prosecutors receive
evidence rather than a resolution written for television.

Bosak and Mentzen are forced to distance Konfederacja from their own deputy.
Braun still gains followers who admire the defiance, but he must build his
martyrdom against a record of injured people and broken rules.

- @poland_event_queue: Place the evidentiary record on the events desk

@braun_front
title: Build a broad anti-fascist front around the expulsion
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Give Jewish organisations and democratic parties a common answer; Braun will call the mobilisation proof of persecution.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Left cannot sustain a national mobilisation.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; progressive_credibility += 4; minority_safety += 6; ko_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 2; far_right_agenda += 3; braun_martyrdom += 4; braun_legal_preparation += 2; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "A democratic front confronts Braun and amplifies his counter-rally"

Jewish organisations, trade unions and the democratic clubs stand together
outside the Sejm and demand Braun's exclusion from public life. People who
watched the ceremony become targets receive a public answer larger than a
procedural reprimand.

Braun answers with a counter-rally and a donation appeal. The front protects a
minority and gives his grievance a national opponent; both consequences were
contained in the decision.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the democratic front to the events desk

@braun_ignore
title: Deny the provocation another week of attention
subtitle: Keep Lewica out of Braun's publicity cycle; leave victims and Konfederacja's leaders to define what silence means.
on-arrival: media_capacity -= 2; minority_safety -= 3; public_trust -= 2; konf_braunist_share += 5; braun_martyrdom += 2; braun_legal_preparation -= 2 if braun_legal_preparation >= 2; news_headline = "Silence leaves Braun's own channels to define the attack"

Our spokespeople move on and the national broadcast cycle shortens. So does
the public defence of the guests who were attacked. They hear that avoiding
Braun's trap mattered more than naming what happened to them.

His channels keep the only uninterrupted version of the film, while Mentzen
and Bosak escape a sustained demand to choose. We deny the provocation our
stage and leave him his own.

- @poland_event_queue: Close the Sejm file and return to the events desk

@december_public_media
