= June 2024 — A death, an arrest and an order nobody trusts

Mateusz Sitek, a twenty-one-year-old soldier, has died after being stabbed
through the barrier on the Belarusian frontier. His comrades and family hear a
country promising that uniforms will never again be left legally exposed.
PSL leader Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz demands protection for the services.

A separate case over soldiers detained after firing warning shots exposes the
other failure: confused orders, commanders protecting themselves and young
personnel discovering the legal rule only after an incident. Asylum seekers
and aid workers fear that a law written in grief will remove individual
accountability altogether.

Lewica arrives with **[+ border_doctrine +]**. [+ border_consequence_summary +]
[? if border_permission_pressure < 40: Earlier restraint leaves room to write
protection and review into the same rule.?][? if border_permission_pressure >=
40 and border_permission_pressure < 70: Public pressure is strong enough that
every safeguard will be attacked as hesitation.?][? if
border_permission_pressure >= 70: The political demand is no longer for clear
orders but for permission broad enough that almost no use of force is
questioned.?]

- @border_doctrine
- @border_immunity
- @border_rights

@border_doctrine
title: Write clear force rules, body-camera duties and independent review
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Give officers an order they can follow and families a review they need not beg the same command to conduct.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Left lacks a defence-and-law team.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; border_doctrine = "Clear force rules with independent review"; military_trust += 5; police_trust += 3; border_security_confidence += 4; border_rights_standard += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; border_permission_pressure -= 4; news_headline = "Protection and accountability enter one border doctrine"

Serving officers, military lawyers and rights monitors write the force ladder
together. Body-camera duties preserve what happened; an outside review means a
commander cannot settle the legality of his own order.

Sitek's comrades receive rules which do not ask them to choose between safety
and prosecution in a second. Aid workers and asylum lawyers retain a place to
challenge abuse after the uniformed chain has acted.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the lawful force doctrine on the events desk

@border_immunity
title: Back the widest officer-protection law
subtitle: Answer grief with a broad immunity presumption; reassure the services while moving the risk onto civilians beyond the barrier.
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "Broad officer immunity"; military_trust += 6; border_security_confidence += 5; border_rights_standard -= 7; minority_safety -= 4; refugee_empathy -= 5; psl_relation += 2; pis_relation += 3; far_right_agenda += 2; border_permission_pressure += 8; news_headline = "The coalition follows the public demand for wider immunity"

We support a presumption that soldiers and Border Guard officers acting at the
frontier will not face prosecution for force used under an operational order.
Units hear the state take their side and the families' anger finds an immediate
law.

The breadth which reassures the services also narrows the path for an injured
civilian to be heard. PiS and PSL welcome our movement; refugee organisations
record that accountability was the part of the doctrine surrendered.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the immunity law on the events desk

@border_rights
title: Oppose immunity and defend asylum access without qualification
subtitle: Refuse to let Sitek's death erase asylum and individual liability; many soldiers will hear principle without protection.
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "Unqualified opposition to force expansion"; progressive_credibility += 5; minority_safety += 5; military_trust -= 7; border_security_confidence -= 7; public_trust -= 5; konf_poll_momentum += 0.5; far_right_agenda += 5; border_permission_pressure += 3; news_headline = "A principled rights stand meets an overwhelmingly hostile climate"

Our caucus rejects the immunity bill and says that asylum law and individual
liability survive even at a violent frontier. Aid groups and minority
organisations hear a party unwilling to make rights conditional on the latest
headline.

Sitek's comrades hear no operational protection offered in its place.
Konfederacja turns the gap into a charge that Lewica will defend everyone
except the people ordered to guard the border.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the rights stand to the events desk

