}
Q.suwerenna_merger_result = "Early walkout; no merger vote";
Q.news_headline = "Suwerenna Polska walks out before the merger talks";
!}

= June 2024 — Suwerenna Polska walks out

**Patryk Jaki** does not wait for the autumn. With **Zbigniew Ziobro** ill and
the merger timetable stretching past every date the party was promised, the
vice-president tells a Wednesday-morning club meeting that Suwerenna Polska
will not spend another six months being absorbed by instalments.

The deputies leave the United Right together. They keep their mandates, the
party keeps its registration, and Solidarna Polska — the name nobody has
bothered to change on the paperwork — remains what it has always legally been.
**Jarosław Kaczyński** learns of the walkout from a statement rather than a
telephone call, which is most of what the walkout was for.

For Lewica the arithmetic is unchanged and the map is not. There is now a
hard-right party in the Sejm that answers to nobody in PiS, carrying the whole
record of Ziobro's Justice Ministry and no longer able to shelter behind a
larger partner.

- @suwerenna_walkout_acknowledge
- @suwerenna_walkout_attack

@suwerenna_walkout_acknowledge
title: Recognise the new independent party
subtitle: Treat the walkout as a real organisational separation
on-arrival: suwerenna_merge_dissent += 1; pis_relation -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica recognises Suwerenna Polska as a separate right-wing party"

We say the plain thing: there are two right-wing parties now where there was
one, they will compete for the same voters, and we intend to treat them as what
they are rather than as one conspiracy with two offices.

It costs nothing and it irritates both of them. Kaczyński would prefer the
walkout described as a tantrum inside the family; Jaki would prefer a rupture
on principle. Calling it an ordinary party split denies each of them the story
he wanted.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the separation

@suwerenna_walkout_attack
title: Attack the walkout's record and programme
subtitle: Keep the new party independent while demanding accountability
on-arrival: suwerenna_merge_dissent += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; pis_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica attacks the record behind the Suwerenna walkout"

We greet the new party with its own inheritance: the disciplinary chambers, the
prosecutors moved for their verdicts, the Justice Fund and the years in which
Ziobro's ministry treated the courts as an annexe of the campaign. A fresh
letterhead does not start a fresh record.

Jaki answers, not unreasonably, that we are describing a period rather than a
party eight days old. His deputies close ranks around precisely the record we
hoped to make them disown, and the walkout acquires the founding grievance it
was missing on Wednesday.

- @poland_event_queue: File the accountability demand

@suwerenna_merger_talks_2024
