= September 2024 — A junior partner prices its disappearance

Zbigniew Ziobro remains the ill leader of Suwerenna Polska while party
vice-president Patryk Jaki negotiates its future. Jarosław Kaczyński wants one
PiS organisation after the loss of government, but his party must decide how
many vice-presidencies, list places, debts and local branches arrive with the
justice-ministry network.

Lewica has no vote in either party. We can give Jaki an outside policy success,
make Ziobro's record the public price of absorption, or publish the terms and
let their members own the choice. October will still belong to the two
organisations; September decides the pressure under which they meet.

- @suwerenna_merger_social
- @suwerenna_merger_attack
- @suwerenna_merger_observe

@suwerenna_merger_social
title: Offer a victim-protection and social-policy concession across the aisle
subtitle: A proposed concession lowers merger pressure; only a later government act can improve household security.
on-arrival: suwerenna_merge_support -= 5; suwerenna_merge_dissent += 3; government_favors += 1; household_policy_pressure += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; pis_relation += 2; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "Party-to-party channel"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "A narrow policy concession gives Suwerenna Polska an outside option"

Our parliamentary channel offers Jaki a narrow victim-protection and household
package he can support without a PiS merger. Suwerenna politicians gain a way
to show their members that a separate organisation can still produce a result.

Nothing has been implemented: another party has conditionally agreed to pursue
the proposal, and the competent government and Sejm must still act. Progressive
members ask why preserving Ziobro's vehicle deserved even that opening.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the proposed concession on the events desk

@suwerenna_merger_attack
title: Publicly make the Ziobro record the price of a PiS merger
subtitle: The attack raises internal dissent but can also harden the smaller party.
on-arrival: suwerenna_merge_support -= 4; suwerenna_merge_dissent += 10; progressive_credibility += 3; pis_relation -= 4; far_right_agenda += 2; news_headline = "Lewica turns the proposed merger into an argument about the justice record"

We put prosecutors, disciplinary courts and the blocked European funds beside
every promised vice-presidency. PiS candidates are asked whether absorbing
Jaki's organisation means accepting common responsibility for Ziobro's term at
Justice.

Some PiS officials become less willing to pay the price. Suwerenna activists
hear an attempt to erase them through prosecution and rally around the very
identity the attack was meant to make toxic.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the justice-record attack to the events desk

@suwerenna_merger_observe
title: Publish the organisational terms and let both parties vote
subtitle: Transparency favours the negotiated historical route; Lewica selects no leader.
on-arrival: suwerenna_merge_support += 12; suwerenna_merge_dissent -= 3; media_capacity += 2; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "The merger terms reach members before either leadership can declare victory"

Our media team obtains and publishes the proposed offices, branch rules and
legal timetable without endorsing them. Members of both parties can see what
their leaders mean by unity before a staged convention declares it complete.

The disclosure reduces rumours and makes a negotiated merger easier to defend.
Lewica gains a clear record and declines the fantasy that clever commentary can
choose Kaczyński's or Jaki's organisation for them.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the published terms on the events desk

