    (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.16 +
    (Number(Q.organiser_energy) || 0) * 0.12;
if (Q.movement_origin_strategy == "Autonomous legal and safety network") {
    movementLeverage += 10;
}
if (Q.movement_origin_strategy == "Party-led mobilisation") {
    movementLeverage -= 8;
}
if (Q.abortion_strategy == "Free vote with constituency pressure") {
    movementLeverage += 5;
}
if (Q.coalition_break_threat) {
    movementLeverage += 4;
}
Q.movement_leverage = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(movementLeverage))
);
Q.movement_reckoning_status = Q.abortion_law_enacted
    ? "A signed law whose practical access must be enforced"
    : (Q.abortion_presidential_action == "Presidential veto"
        ? "A parliamentary victory stopped by presidential veto"
        : (Q.abortion_presidential_action ==
                "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal"
            ? "A parliamentary victory frozen by constitutional referral"
            : "A bill defeated in the Sejm"));
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += -4;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_left_ownership += -6;
Q.news_headline = Q.abortion_law_enacted
    ? "Organisers demand evidence that the signed law works"
    : "Organisers demand a route beyond the blocked abortion bill";
!}

= August 2024 — Political support does not mean party control

Marta Lempart and the organisers of the All-Poland Women's Strike have read the
full July chain beside Lewica MP Katarzyna Kotula. Its status is **[+
movement_reckoning_status +]**. They remember the Tribunal ruling, the deaths
in hospitals, the marches and every promise to turn support into access.

[? if movement_leverage >= 65: They arrive as an autonomous force with local
organisers, public trust and the ability to make refusal costly.?][? if
movement_leverage >= 38 and movement_leverage < 65: They still have a national
voice, but need party and parliamentary allies for the next institutional
step.?][? if movement_leverage < 38: Exhaustion and earlier party control have
left the movement dependent on the same leadership it is meant to audit.?]

In 2020 the Left built **[+ movement_origin_strategy +]**. In April it chose
**[+ abortion_strategy +]**. Those histories decide whether ministers are
hearing from autonomous partners, disappointed campaign auxiliaries or a
network the party once told to go home.

The movement asks for something enforceable: practical access now, a lawful
route past the remaining veto point, political power of its own, or an honest
admission that the party intends to absorb the campaign.

- @movement_clinical
- @movement_deadline
- @movement_candidates
- @movement_capture

@movement_clinical
