The signatures sit beneath funded housing and health milestones, an abortion
vote date and a clause allowing Razem to oppose the government outside that
programme. Zandberg postpones the departure because the paper now contains
dates and money, not another appeal to unity. KO and PSL see a second coalition
agreement written for a party which still reserves the right to vote against
them.

The SLD barons resent the enforceable veto, while Wiosna veterans accept the
price of unity. Labour and the progressives claim the funded milestones and
rights deadline; PPS treats the appeal clause as a useful guarantee that a
smaller socialist partner can remain itself.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the signed support protocol on the events desk

