social spending and civil rights. The members vote as they were going to vote,
and **[+ ko_primary_2024_surname +]** wins anyway — but part of that mandate is
now read through our intervention. Progressives inside KO feel less isolated;
Tusk's apparatus accuses us of treating their members as an electorate we are
entitled to manage.

The nominee begins the campaign with a stronger left-facing wing and a colder
relationship with the party that helped make it visible.

- @poland_event_queue: Put KO's irritated result on the events desk

@ko_incumbent_compact
title: Back Trzaskowski's re-election for a written social and rights compact
subtitle: Share an incumbent's campaign in exchange for commitments he must defend from the Palace.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski"; pres_2025_incumbent = 1; ko_relation += 6; president_relation += 5; labor_credibility += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; trz_right_backlash += 4; pis_cohabitation_rally += 3; news_headline = "Trzaskowski seeks re-election with a negotiated social and rights compact"

The President signs a campaign compact on labour law, housing and civil
rights, and Lewica agrees to defend his re-election. Five years of vetoes,
appointments and public interventions become a shared record rather than KO's
alone. Our negotiators gain access to the Palace campaign; our own candidate
would now struggle to explain whom the Left ultimately wants to win.

PiS welcomes the clarity. It can present Trzaskowski not as a referee seeking
another term, but as the head of a democratic coalition with Lewica written
into its programme.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the presidential compact on the events desk

@ko_incumbent_distance
title: Let the incumbent run on his record and preserve a separate Left campaign
subtitle: Keep Lewica's nomination and make five years in the Palace answer for themselves.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski"; pres_2025_incumbent = 1; party_unity += 3; ko_relation -= 5; president_relation -= 2; razem_cooperation += 3; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses to become the incumbent President's campaign annex"

Lewica congratulates Trzaskowski and declines the common platform. His vetoes,
appointments and compromises will be defended by his own campaign; our
nominee remains free to say where an allied President fell short. Razem and
party organisers gain a reason to work under one banner instead of becoming
canvassers for KO.

The Palace reads the distance as ingratitude after years of cohabitation. A
second-round conversation remains possible, but it will begin without the
trust a first-round compact might have bought.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the separate campaign on the events desk

