The referral asks for the board minutes, the margin approvals and the
correspondence with the ministry that supervises the Treasury's stake. Not the
price — the decision to set it.

Nobody notices in September. The finding lands in the following year, when a
different cabinet holds the same supervisory powers and has to explain why it
is not using them differently.

