= 10 October 2023 — Two resignations, five days out

General **Rajmund Andrzejczak**, Chief of the General Staff, and General
**Tomasz Piotrowski**, Operational Commander of the Armed Forces, resign
together five days before the parliamentary election. Neither man gives a
public reason beyond the impossibility of continuing. The defence ministry
briefs that the departures are personal; officers brief that the command has
spent months being contradicted in public by political appointees while a war
runs along the border.

The Constitution keeps the armed forces neutral and under civilian control,
which is exactly why this is dangerous in both directions. A government may
lawfully lose confidence in its generals. A government five days from an
election, on a frontier state's eastern flank, with no successor named and no
explanation offered, has produced a hole in the chain of command that no
campaign message closes.

[? if left_in_government = 1: We share cabinet responsibility, so our defence
and interior people will be asked what they knew and when, and any answer that
sounds like a party line will be quoted for years.?][? if left_in_government =
0: We hold no portfolio and no access to the operational picture. We can demand
the record, protect the officers from becoming a campaign prop, or make this
the closing argument about competence.?]

[? if opposition_infosec_committee = 1: The joint opposition committee that has
been meeting since the 2021 mailbox leak is the only forum in which three
caucuses can sign one security document inside a week.?]
[? if security_incident_pressure >= 10: This lands on a security record that
already includes the missile at Przewodów and the border emergency, and the
public has stopped treating each of them as isolated.?]

- @defence_command_record
- @defence_command_campaign
- @defence_command_neutral
- @defence_command_joint

