We ask the narrow question: who holds classified access inside the judicial
system, who granted it, when was it last reviewed, and what happens when a
holder travels. It is the question the services would ask themselves, which is
why it produces an answer instead of a headline.

Reviews of this kind always find more than the case that triggered them. Some
of what it finds will embarrass judges we have defended for years, and we have
just committed ourselves to publishing the standard rather than the exception.

- @poland_event_queue: Order the clearance question

