We put the whole recording up ourselves, uncut, with a short note: this is
what a party arguing about its own record sounds like, and the alternative is
a party that does not argue. Younger members and organisers respond to it
better than to any communications strategy of the previous year.

The people we named do not respond well at all. Two coalition partners now
know precisely how our deputies rate their ministers, and they will price that
into the next negotiation rather than the next press conference.

