We stop discussing the arrest and start publishing the grants: which victim
support organisations applied, which were refused, which received money for
purposes unrelated to victims, and which parish, foundation or association
received a fire engine instead. The audit chamber gets a formal request.

It is the version of this scandal that reaches people who do not care which
deputy was detained. It is also slower than the case, and it will still be
producing findings long after the courts have decided whether anybody is
guilty of anything.

