= August 2024 — A subsidy is not an entitlement

The State Electoral Commission rejects the governing-then-opposition party's
2023 campaign financial report. Ministries, state companies and public media
spent public money on what the commission finds was campaign activity, and the
statutory consequence is a reduction of the party's public subsidy and
campaign reimbursement running to tens of millions of złoty.

Public party funding exists so that parties do not have to be bought. A
commission cutting it is therefore doing exactly what it was built to do — and
doing it to the largest opposition party, in a state where half the political
class disputes which institutions are legitimate.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Our coalition benefits directly and will be
accused, credibly enough for its own voters, of having arranged it.?][? if
left_in_government = 0: We benefit from nothing here except the precedent, and
the precedent applies to us as well.?]

[? if referendum_2023_stance = "Campaign-finance challenge": The file the
commission is ruling on is, in part, the one our lawyers opened in September
2023 while everybody else was arguing about whether to take the second
ballot.?]
[? if referendum_2023_stance = "Audit chamber referral": The audit chamber's
finding on the referendum's public spending is cited in the commission's
reasoning, which makes the 2023 referral the most productive paperwork this
party has ever filed.?]
[? if party_finance_scandal >= 20: We have already put campaign-finance
material on the record this cycle, which makes our position consistent and our
motives easier to attribute.?]

- @pkw_funding_standard
- @pkw_funding_press
- @pkw_funding_restraint
- @pkw_funding_origin

