= February 2024 — A calendar is also a position

Sejm Marshal <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> announces that the four abortion bills
will not be scheduled before the local elections in April. His reason is
delivered in the tone of a man explaining something obvious: the campaign is
heated, the subject is divisive, and everyone would benefit from calm.

He controls the order paper, so this is not a proposal. It is a decision, taken
by the office that decides, and it postpones the one thing this coalition
promised that cannot be delivered by an ordinance.

**Anna Maria Żukowska**, the Left's parliamentary club chair, answers in
public and does not soften it: *wypierdalaj z tym spokojem*. The clip is
everywhere within an hour. It is coarse, it is aimed at a coalition partner
holding the second office in the state, and among the women who spent 2020 in
the street it is the most popular sentence any coalition politician has said
since the government formed.

[? if movement_reckoning_status = "": The movement has not yet been given a
deadline by us, which means it has nothing to hold us to and nothing to lose by
walking away.?]
[? if abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1: We have already put a cabinet deadline on
this, which the Marshal has now overrun in public.?]
[? if left_holds_marshal = 1: We hold the Marshal's chair ourselves in this
timeline, which makes the postponement a decision of ours to defend or
reverse.?]
[? if p2050_relation < 40: Relations with Poland 2050 are already poor enough
that this reads as the beginning of something rather than a scheduling
dispute.?]

- @delay_back_zukowska
- @delay_schedule
- @delay_deadline
- @delay_accept

@delay_back_zukowska
title: Stand behind the language and let it be the Left's position
subtitle: The most-heard thing the Left says all year; it makes a coalition partner an enemy over a date.
on-arrival: {!
Q.abortion_delay_response = "Backed the language";
Q.feminist_trust = (Number(Q.feminist_trust) || 50) + 8;
Q.movement_autonomy = (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) + 4;
Q.womens_strike_activist_mobilisation =
    (Number(Q.womens_strike_activist_mobilisation) || 0) + 7;
Q.progressive_credibility =
    (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) + 5;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 4;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.2;
Q.p2050_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 41) - 8
);
Q.psl_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 45) - 5
);
Q.government_coalition_dissent =
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 6;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left refuses to apologise for how the postponement was answered";
!}

We do not issue a clarification. The club chair said what a very large number
of women have been saying since October 2020, and a coalition that expects
patience on this subject can hear it in the register in which it is felt.

Two partners now believe the Left will attack them personally rather than
negotiate, and they are not entirely wrong. What we have bought is the one
thing money cannot: the movement's belief that somebody in this government is
not managing them.

- @poland_event_queue: Let the answer stand

@delay_schedule
title: Use the chair ourselves and put the bills on the order paper
subtitle: Requires holding the Marshal's chair. Ends the delay by exercising the office rather than complaining about it.
choose-if: left_holds_marshal = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Marshal's chair belongs to Poland 2050 in this timeline — the order paper is not ours to write.
on-arrival: {!
Q.abortion_delay_response = "Scheduled by our own chair";
Q.abortion_delay_months = 0;
Q.abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1;
Q.feminist_trust = (Number(Q.feminist_trust) || 50) + 10;
Q.movement_autonomy = (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) + 3;
Q.progressive_credibility =
    (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) + 6;
Q.p2050_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 41) - 6
);
Q.psl_relation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 45) - 8
);
Q.government_coalition_dissent =
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 9;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The bills are scheduled by a Marshal who does not want them postponed";
!}

The chair is ours, so the order paper is ours. The first readings are set for
March and the coalition discovers that the office it treated as a courtesy
title has a calendar attached.

PSL's deputies say openly that they were not consulted, which is true, and that
they will vote accordingly, which is also true. We have converted a
postponement into a vote we may lose — and a vote that happens is worth more to
the people waiting for this law than a date that keeps moving.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the order paper

@delay_deadline
title: Accept the delay and convert it into a written coalition deadline
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Trades the argument for a date the partners have to sign.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party has no negotiating capacity free to turn a postponement into a signed timetable.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.abortion_delay_response = "Written deadline";
Q.abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1;
Q.abortion_delay_months = 2;
Q.p2050_relation = (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 41) + 4;
Q.psl_relation = (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 45) + 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 2
);
Q.feminist_trust = (Number(Q.feminist_trust) || 50) + 2;
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 2
);
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The postponement is traded for a signed date after the local elections";
!}

We take the delay and charge for it. The coalition council minutes a date, the
Marshal's office confirms it in writing, and every leader signs — which turns a
gesture of goodwill into a document that can be produced in July.

The organisers are unimpressed and say so. Their position is that a signature
from this coalition has a poor record, and the only honest answer we have is
that we agree and took it anyway.

- @poland_event_queue: File the signed timetable

@delay_accept
title: Accept the postponement and keep the coalition quiet
subtitle: The least costly answer this month and the one the movement remembers longest.
on-arrival: {!
Q.abortion_delay_response = "Accepted";
Q.abortion_delay_months =
    (Number(Q.abortion_delay_months) || 2) + 2;
Q.p2050_relation = (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 41) + 5;
Q.psl_relation = (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 45) + 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 4
);
Q.feminist_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.feminist_trust) || 50) - 9
);
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 6
);
Q.womens_strike_party_conversion = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.womens_strike_party_conversion) || 0) - 5
);
Q.progressive_credibility = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) - 5
);
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left accepts the postponement and asks the movement for patience";
!}

The club is told to lower the temperature, the language is walked back, and the
coalition's spring proceeds without an argument about the one subject that
brought several hundred thousand people onto the street four years ago.

Local elections are won and lost on other things. What is spent here is not
measured in April; it is measured in July, when the vote finally happens, and
in whether anybody outside the party still believes we intended to hold it.

- @poland_event_queue: Ask the movement for patience
